        <senderName>Environment Canada</senderName>
        <headline>red warning - tornado - in effect</headline>
        <description>At 7:26 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Friday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for Southwestern Ontario. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: Windsor, Essex and Chatham-Kent. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking an area of severe thunderstorms that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible.</description>
        <instruction>Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</instruction>
        <web>https://weather.gc.ca/</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:EC-MSC-SMC:1.0:Alert_Type</valueName>
